From: iHost add-on contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Route pinned host-configured upstream DNS through host routing

Use the existing OTBR POSIX configuration header; preserve compiler flags.
Adapt the host-scoped resolver policy accepted in OpenThread PR #13545
(commit 82eb4863ade08819cf35c28ff3c8bb9f93a06213), without importing its
newer IPv6/RDNSS resolver machinery into the pinned Silicon Labs SDK.

--- a/util/third_party/ot-br-posix/src/agent/openthread-otbr-posix-config.h.in
+++ b/util/third_party/ot-br-posix/src/agent/openthread-otbr-posix-config.h.in
@@ -51,4 +51,15 @@
     "@PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR@/third_party/openthread/repo/src/posix/platform/openthread.conf.example"
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * Host-configured DNS servers must follow the host routing table. In particular,
+ * Supervisor DNS can be reached through a bridge rather than the Thread backbone.
+ * This pinned resolver has no RDNSS server path. OpenThread PR #13545 separately
+ * preserves infra binding for RDNSS in newer versions; revisit on SDK upgrades.
+ * https://github.com/openthread/openthread/pull/13545
+ */
+#ifndef OPENTHREAD_POSIX_CONFIG_UPSTREAM_DNS_BIND_TO_INFRA_NETIF
+#define OPENTHREAD_POSIX_CONFIG_UPSTREAM_DNS_BIND_TO_INFRA_NETIF 0
+#endif
+
 #endif // OPENTHREAD_OTBR_POSIX_CONFIG_H_
